### Part B — Brain Backup

#### Step 5 — Setup git in brain folder (idempotent — first run only)

```bash
cd /Users/agent/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup

# Only if brain/.git doesn't exist
if [ ! -d brain/.git ]; then
  cd brain
  git init
  # Use HTTPS + fine-grained PAT (not SSH) — scheduled-task env can't access ssh-agent
  TOKEN=$(cat /Users/agent/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/secrets/github-pat-brain-backup.txt 2>/dev/null)
  if [ -n "$TOKEN" ]; then
    git remote add origin "https://x-access-token:${TOKEN}@github.com/immersepe12/mindtalk-brain-backup.git" 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
  unset TOKEN
  cd ..
fi
```

**Backup repo:** https://github.com/immersepe12/mindtalk-brain-backup (created 2026-06-15)

**Authentication (set up 2026-06-22):** Uses GitHub fine-grained Personal Access Token (PAT), NOT SSH. Reason: Cowork's scheduled-task environment does not inherit the macOS Keychain ssh-agent, so SSH-based pushes fail silently in scheduled context (hit this wall 2026-06-16 → 2026-06-21, 6 days running). HTTPS+PAT works headless.

**PAT location:** `/Users/agent/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/secrets/github-pat-brain-backup.txt` (chmod 600)
**Token scope:** Fine-grained PAT, scoped to `immersepe12/mindtalk-brain-backup` only, permissions: Contents Read+Write
**Token rotation:** Annually (or whenever the file's mtime is >330 days old — T16 should warn at 330 days)
**Token embedded in remote URL:** `.git/config` contains the token in the origin URL. File is `chmod 600`; repo is private.

If push fails despite PAT being present, post Slack flag — the token may have expired or been revoked.

#### Step 6 — Commit + push

```bash
cd /Users/agent/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/brain
git add -A
git status --porcelain > /tmp/brain-changes.txt
CHANGE_COUNT=$(wc -l < /tmp/brain-changes.txt)

if [ $CHANGE_COUNT -gt 0 ]; then
  git commit -m "auto: brain snapshot $(date +%F-%H%M) | $CHANGE_COUNT files changed"

  # Self-healing: if push fails on auth, try refreshing remote URL with current PAT from file
  if ! git push origin main 2>&1 | tee /tmp/push-result.txt; then
    if grep -qi "auth\|permission\|403\|401" /tmp/push-result.txt; then
      TOKEN=$(cat /Users/agent/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/secrets/github-pat-brain-backup.txt 2>/dev/null)
      if [ -n "$TOKEN" ]; then
        git remote set-url origin "https://x-access-token:${TOKEN}@github.com/immersepe12/mindtalk-brain-backup.git"
        git push origin main 2>&1
      fi
      unset TOKEN
    fi
  fi
fi
```

**PAT rotation procedure** (for Kushal — keep this in the spec for future-self reference):
1. Revoke old PAT at https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta
2. Generate new fine-grained PAT, same settings (mindtalk-brain-backup repo only, Contents R+W, 1yr expiry)
3. Edit `secrets/github-pat-brain-backup.txt` with new token via editor (NOT terminal, to keep it out of shell history)
4. Test: `cd brain && TOKEN=$(cat ../secrets/github-pat-brain-backup.txt) && git remote set-url origin "https://x-access-token:${TOKEN}@github.com/immersepe12/mindtalk-brain-backup.git" && git push origin main && unset TOKEN`

#### Step 7 — Track backup history

Append to `brain/memory/backup-history.md`:
```
{TIMESTAMP} | {CHANGE_COUNT} files changed | commit: {SHA} | push: {success/skipped}
```

