### Part B2 — Production push-state check (added 2026-07-10 after the Day-9 push freeze)

Every night, verify the main site repo is not silently frozen:

```bash
cd /Users/agent/Documents/GitHub/mindtalk
LOCAL=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
PAT=$(grep -o "github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]*" /Users/agent/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/secrets/github-pat-brain-backup.txt | head -1)
REMOTE=$(git ls-remote "https://x-access-token:${PAT}@github.com/immersepe12/mindtalk.git" main | cut -f1)
```

- If `LOCAL == REMOTE` → healthy, note `push-state: in-sync` in the Slack digest.
- If `LOCAL != REMOTE` AND local has commits not on remote (`git log ${REMOTE}..HEAD --oneline` non-empty) → **production is frozen. Self-heal: push with the PAT** (`git push "https://x-access-token:${PAT}@github.com/immersepe12/mindtalk.git" main`), re-verify, and log `push-state: HEALED via PAT` to Slack. The brain-backup PAT has verified push access to the main repo (2026-07-10).
- If the PAT push also fails → 🚨 Slack escalate `PRODUCTION FROZEN — {N} commits stuck locally` with the exact commit list. This must never again sit undetected for 9 days.
- Also check for stale locks: if `.git/index.lock` exists and is >2 hours old, attempt removal; if sandbox can't remove it, tell Kushal the exact `rm` command in the digest.

### Part B3 — Weekly ship-velocity check (added 2026-07-10; runs Sunday only)

On Sundays, count pages that went LIVE this week (tracking-db entries with `published_at` in the last 7 days AND verified 200, plus T9/stub-pilot week logs):

- If live pages < 8 (T9 escalation floor Kushal set 2026-07-03) for the week → include `⚠ VELOCITY: {N}/20 live this week — below 8/wk escalation floor` in the Slack digest with the top blocking reason (vetoes / caps / push / brief starvation).
- If live pages < floor for 2 consecutive weeks → flag `SYSTEM UNDERUTILISED` per GOALS.md and instruct Meta-Learner (runs 2h earlier — so write the flag to `brain/BACKLOG.md` operational items for next Sunday's Meta-Learner) to propose either loosening filters or raising discovery/brief throughput.
- Also check brief runway: count tracking-db `BRIEF_CREATED`. If < 15, flag `⚠ BRIEF RUNWAY LOW: {N} unshipped briefs — T9 will starve within a week` in the digest.

